# Owner: Nati — Live Data List & Moderation (full-stack)

You own **the list of the live data** and its moderation — front and back. This is
the "watch the data pour in" screen and the home of the anti-poisoning /
flag-outlier story.

You read the shared `reports` table (Gezachew owns its migration — coordinate the
row shape day one). Read `000`, `010`, `020`, `040` first.

## Backend (your half)

- `app/Http/Controllers/ReportController.php@index` — `GET /reports`: newest-first
  reports, joined with the agent name, shaped via an **API Resource** (camelCase).
- `@flag` — `POST /reports/{id}/flag`: set `is_flagged = true`. Flagged rows are
  **excluded from Tsegaye's aggregates** — coordinate so `SnapshotService`
  honors it (the exclusion query lives in his engine; your job is to set the flag
  and expose it).

```ts
interface ReportRowData {
  id: number;
  crop: 'teff' | 'coffee';
  market: 'adama' | 'addis_ababa' | 'jimma';
  price: number;
  reportedAt: string;    // ISO
  source: 'official' | 'crowd';
  agentName: string;     // attribution
  isFlagged: boolean;
  createdAt: string;
}
```

## Frontend (your half)

- `resources/js/Pages/Reports.tsx` (route `GET /reports`),
  `Components/RecentReportsFeed.tsx`, `Components/ReportRow.tsx` (share the row
  with Gezachew's "my recent entries").
- Each row: crop, market, price, reported-at, source, **agent who entered it**,
  and a **flag** control. Flagged rows render struck/dimmed.
- Filters (client-side is fine): by crop, by market, "flagged only" toggle.

## Live update (LOCKED: polling)

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(() => router.reload({ only: ['reports'] }), 2500);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, []);
```

New rows slide/highlight in so the audience sees data arriving as Gezachew submits.

## Flag-outlier (the anti-poisoning beat)

A flag button → `POST /reports/{id}/flag`. Flag a fake low price and watch the
dashboard's price/confidence self-correct — a strong live moment. Wire the button
and set the flag; Tsegaye's engine excludes flagged rows.

## Don't

- Don't recompute aggregates — you show raw reports; the dashboard shows the
  aggregate.
- Don't paginate heavily; newest ~50 rows is plenty for the demo.
